  "verbalization": "Terbutaline, a bronchodilator, is linked to Neuropilin-2 through a series of molecular interactions. The evidence suggests that terbutaline acts as a target of a compound, MIP, which in turn is targeted by another compound, (3R)-5,8,9-trimethoxy-2,2-dimethyl-3,4-dihydropyrano[2,3-b]quinolin-3-ol, and later by (5R,8R,9R,10R,13R,14R,17S)-17-[(2R)-5-(2-hydroxypropan-2-yl)-2-methyloxolan-2-yl]-4,4,8,10,14-pentamethyl-1,2,5,6,7,9,11,12,13,15,16,17-dodecahydrocyclopenta[a]phenanthren-3-one. All these compounds share a common target, Neuropilin-2, indicating a potential pathway where terbutaline may influence Neuropilin-2 through these intermediates. The evidence suggests a possible mechanism involving the targeting of Neuropilin-2 by a series of compounds that are themselves targets of other molecules, possibly through a regulatory or signaling pathway. The integration of these pathways highlights the complexity of the relationship between terbutaline and Neuropilin-2, emphasizing the role of intermediates in mediating the interaction.",
